	<!-- TemplateBeginEditable name="About-BoardGame" -->
    <div class="container pt-5 pb-5">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="col-lg-6">
				<h2>About Settlers of Catan</h2>
				<p>
					Catan, also known as Settlers of Catan, is a multiplayer board game where players compete to build settlements on an uncharted island: 
				</p>
				
				<strong>Goal</strong>
				
				<p>
					Players collect resources, trade with opponents, and build roads, settlements, and cities to earn victory points. 
					The first player to reach a set number of victory points wins.
				</p>
				
				<strong>Gameplay</strong>
				
				<p>
					Players roll dice to collect resources based on the terrain hexes on the board. 
					The board is made up of hexagonal tiles that create an island with mountains, pastures, hills, fields, and forests. 
				</p>
				
				<strong>Design</strong>
				
				<p>
					The game was designed by Klaus Teuber and was first published in Germany in 1995. Teuber was inspired by the Viking settlers and thought that if any civilization could find the fictional island of Catan, it would be the Vikings. 
				</p>
				
				<strong>Features</strong>
				
				<p>
					The game is intended for three or four players ages 10 and up, and each round can take up to 90 minutes. 
					The board is variable, so each game is different.			
				</p>
			</div>
			
			<div class="col-lg-6">
				<img class="tcg-logo" src="../images/boardgame_img/settlers-of-catan/catan_cards.png" alt="Resources">
	
				<blockquote style="max-width: 401px;"><h3>Would you like to trade your two sheeps  for my three bricks?</h3></blockquote>

			</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	<!-- TemplateEndEditable -->

	
	<div class="dropdown-divider-content"></div>
	
	<!-- TemplateBeginEditable name="BoardGame-Tutorial" -->
